+Pollard rho / parallel collision search (`pcs.h`):
+======
+`PollardRho<Compare, T>` finds a collision of a step function `f: T -> T`
+via cycle finding. `Compare` decides what a collision is: it gets the two
+preimages and their images, `cmp(a1, f(a1), b1, f(b1))`, so it can also
+reject unwanted collisions (e.g. for flavoured functions).
+
+Usage:
+```c++
+#include "algorithm/pcs.h"
+
+// a collision of f(x) = x^2 + 1 mod p: two distinct preimages, same image
+struct Cmp {
+	bool operator()(const uint32_t &a1, const uint32_t &a2,
+	                const uint32_t &b1, const uint32_t &b2) const noexcept {
+		return (a2 == b2) && (a1 != b1);
+	}
+};
+
+constexpr uint32_t p = 65521;
+const auto f = [](const uint32_t &x) { return uint32_t((uint64_t(x) * x + 1u) % p); };
+const auto flavour = [](const uint32_t &x) { return x; }; // no flavouring
+
+// in: x1 = y1 = start point; out: x1 != y1 with f(x1) == f(y1)
+uint32_t x1 = 2, y1 = 2, x2, y2;
+const bool found = PollardRho<Cmp, uint32_t>::run(f, flavour, x1, y1, x2, y2);
+```
+
+The parallel collision search (`PCS`) is not finished yet.
+More examples: `tests/algorithm/pcs.cpp` (factoring via `src/algorithm/rsa.h`)
+and `src/algorithm/subsetsum.h` (subset sum).
